# A Chrome OS device has no function row: the top row emits *action* keys
# (KEY_BACK, KEY_FORWARD, KEY_BRIGHTNESS{UP,DOWN}, KEY_VOLUME{UP,DOWN}, ...),
# which keyd turns into the XF86 keysyms Omarchy binds. This file tells the
# keybindings menu (bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings) which physical key each of
# those keysyms sits on, so it shows the action row's legends instead of a
# function row this keyboard does not have.
#
# Format: <keysym> <name>, both ^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$; one per line, '#' comments.
XF86MonBrightnessUp F7
XF86MonBrightnessDown F6
XF86AudioRaiseVolume F10
XF86AudioLowerVolume F9
XF86AudioMute F8
